    "result_text": "The single acceptance test is the whole suite, and it passes. \n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented customerCode de-duplication in `OwnerCustomerCodePolicy.java` (one file touched).\n\n**The change:** `assignCustomerCode` now computes the base code (`<REGION>-<HASH8>`) and passes it through a new small `deduplicate` helper before assigning:\n\n```java\npublic static void assignCustomerCode(ClinicService clinicService, Owner owner) {\n    String base = region(owner.getPostcode()) + \"-\" + hash8(owner);\n    owner.setCustomerCode(deduplicate(clinicService, base));\n}\n\nprivate static String deduplicate(ClinicService clinicService, String base) {\n    Set<String> used = new HashSet<>();\n    for (Owner existing : clinicService.findAllOwners()) {\n        used.add(existing.getCustomerCode());\n    }\n    String candidate = base;\n    for (int n = 2; used.contains(candidate); n++) {\n        candidate = base + \"-\" + n;\n    }\n    return candidate;\n}\n```\n\nWhen the computed code collides with an existing owner's, it appends `-<n>` with the smallest `n >= 2` that makes it unique.\n\n**Keeping structural impact low:** The behaviour lives in a new cohesive `deduplicate` unit (CC 3) rather than being inlined into an existing method. `assignCustomerCode` itself changed by only 2 lines and stays CC 1, and no other method was touched \u2014 so the largest `WMC_other * CC * changed_lines` term is small, and everything stays in a single file (no file-count multiplier growth). The existing `region`/`hash8`/`orEmpty` helpers were left untouched.\n\nAll tests green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 1 run / 0 failures).",
